# PIP - File and device transfer

```text
PIP destination=source[,source...]
```

## Syntax

Put the **destination** to the left of the equals sign. For example, copy
all the COM files from A to D with this command:

```
PIP D:=A:*.COM
```

Type `PIP` alone to open the `*` prompt. Enter an assignment there without
repeating the command name. Press Enter on an empty line to leave PIP.

## Selectors

To copy COM files from every user area on B into user 4 on A:

```
PIP A4:=B[-]:*.COM
```

### Duplicate names

A selector can match up to 64 source files. If two distinct selected files
would produce the same destination name, PIP reports the conflict before
copying any of them.

## Examples

1. Copy one file and verify the result:

```
PIP D:BACKUP.COM=A:PROGRAM.COM[V]
```

2. Join two text files in the stated order:

```
PIP D:ALL.TXT=D:ONE.TXT,D:TWO.TXT
```

For source-first syntax, see [COPY](COPY.HLP).
